<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="COL" style="id">COLOSSIANS</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="COL 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Apostolic Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="COL 1:1"/>
    Paul, called to be an apostle of Christ Jesus through God’s sovereign will, and Timothy our brother,
    <verse eid="COL 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="COL 1:2"/>
    To God’s consecrated people and faithful brothers and sisters in Christ who live in Colossae:
    <verse eid="COL 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">May grace or unmerited favour and peace be yours from God our Father.</para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Thanksgiving and Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="COL 1:3"/>
    We continually express gratitude to God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, as we pray for you at all times,
    <verse eid="COL 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="COL 1:4"/>
    since we have received reports about your faith in Christ Jesus and the love you demonstrate towards all of God’s people,
    <verse eid="COL 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="COL 1:5"/>
    on account of the hope that is being kept safe for you in heaven, about which you previously heard when the message of truth—the gospel—was proclaimed to you.
    <verse eid="COL 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="COL 1:6"/>
    This gospel has reached you just as it is producing fruit and growing throughout the entire world—and it has been doing the same among you from the day you first heard and truly understood God’s grace,
    <verse eid="COL 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="COL 1:7"/>
    exactly as you were taught by Epaphras, our dear fellow servant, who serves as a faithful minister of Christ on your behalf,
    <verse eid="COL 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="COL 1:8"/>
    and who has informed us about your love that flows from the Spirit.
    <verse eid="COL 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="COL 1:9"/>
    For this reason, we have not ceased praying for you and asking that you would be filled with the knowledge of His will through complete wisdom and spiritual comprehension,
    <verse eid="COL 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="COL 1:10"/>
    so that you may conduct your lives in a manner that honours the Lord and pleases Him in every respect—bearing fruit through every good work and growing in the knowledge of God,
    <verse eid="COL 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="COL 1:11"/>
    being empowered with complete strength according to His magnificent might, enabling you to attain total endurance and patience accompanied by joy,
    <verse eid="COL 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="COL 1:12"/>
    giving thanks to the Father, who has made you qualified to receive your share of the inheritance belonging to God’s people in the realm of light.
    <verse eid="COL 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="COL 1:13"/>
    He has delivered us from the domain of darkness and brought us into the kingdom of His beloved Son,
    <verse eid="COL 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Preeminence of Christ in Redemption and Creation</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="COL 1:14"/>
    in whom we possess redemption, which is the forgiveness of our sins.
    <verse eid="COL 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="COL 1:15"/>
    He is the visible representation of the invisible God, the firstborn or the supreme One of and over all creation,
    <verse eid="COL 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="COL 1:16"/>
    for in Him all things were brought into existence—things in heaven and things on earth, visible things and invisible things, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or authorities. All things have been created through Him and for Him.
    <verse eid="COL 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="COL 1:17"/>
    He exists prior to all things, and in Him all things hold together in unity.
    <verse eid="COL 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="COL 1:18"/>
    He is the head of the body, which is the church. He is the origin, the firstborn or the supreme One from among the dead, so that He might occupy first place in everything.
    <verse eid="COL 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="COL 1:19"/>
    For it pleased God that all His fullness would take up residence in Him,
    <verse eid="COL 1:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="COL 1:20"/>
    and through Him to reconcile all things to Himself—having established peace through the blood of His cross—yes, through Him—whether things on earth or things in heaven.
    <verse eid="COL 1:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="COL 1:21"/>
    And you, who were once estranged and hostile in your thinking through wicked actions,
    <verse eid="COL 1:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="COL 1:22"/>
    He has now reconciled through His physical body by means of death, in order to present you holy and without blemish and above reproach before Him,
    <verse eid="COL 1:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="COL 1:23"/>
    provided that you remain in the faith, firmly established and unshaken, not shifting away from the hope proclaimed in the gospel you heard, which has been announced to every creature under heaven, and of which I, Paul, have become a servant.
    <verse eid="COL 1:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Purpose of the Sufferings and Ministry of Paul</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="COL 1:24"/>
    Now I find joy in the sufferings I endure for your benefit, and I am completing in my physical body what remains of Christ’s afflictions for the sake of His body, which is the church.
    <verse eid="COL 1:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="COL 1:25"/>
    I became a servant of the church according to the responsibility God gave me for your benefit: to bring God’s word to its full expression,
    <verse eid="COL 1:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="COL 1:26"/>
    the mystery that was concealed throughout past ages and generations but has now been revealed to His consecrated people.
    <verse eid="COL 1:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="COL 1:27"/>
    God determined to make known among the Gentiles the glorious riches of this mystery—which is Christ dwelling in you, your confident hope of glory.
    <verse eid="COL 1:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="COL 1:28"/>
    We proclaim Him, warning every person and instructing every person with complete wisdom, so that we may present every person as perfect or fully mature in Christ.
    <verse eid="COL 1:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="COL 1:29"/>
    For this purpose I labour strenuously, contending according to His power that works mightily within me.
    <verse eid="COL 1:29"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="COL 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="COL 2"/>
  <para style="s1">Christ, the Mystery of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="COL 2:1"/>
    For I want you to understand how intensely I am labouring on behalf of you and those in Laodicea and all who have not met me personally,
    <verse eid="COL 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="COL 2:2"/>
    so that their hearts would be strengthened, being united together in love, and that they would reach the complete wealth that comes from full conviction of understanding, resulting in the knowledge of God’s mystery—which is Christ—
    <verse eid="COL 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="COL 2:3"/>
    in whom all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge lie concealed.
    <verse eid="COL 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="COL 2:4"/>
    I am telling you this so that no one will mislead you with persuasive arguments.
    <verse eid="COL 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="COL 2:5"/>
    For although I am physically absent, I am nevertheless with you in spirit, finding joy as I observe your disciplined manner of life and the solid foundation of your faith in Christ.
    <verse eid="COL 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Fullness of the Deity Dwelling in Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="COL 2:6"/>
    Therefore, just as you received Christ Jesus as Lord, continue living in union with Him,
    <verse eid="COL 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="COL 2:7"/>
    having been rooted and being continually built up in Him and strengthened in the faith just as you were instructed, overflowing in thanksgiving.
    <verse eid="COL 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="COL 2:8"/>
    Be careful that no one takes you captive through philosophy and deceptive emptiness based on human tradition, based on the elementary principles that govern the world, rather than based on Christ.
    <verse eid="COL 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="COL 2:9"/>
    For in Him the complete fullness of deity resides in bodily form.
    <verse eid="COL 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="COL 2:10"/>
    And you have been brought to completion in Him, who is the supreme head over every ruler and authority.
    <verse eid="COL 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="COL 2:11"/>
    In Him you also received a circumcision performed without human hands, through the removal of the body dominated by the flesh, through the circumcision that belongs to Christ.
    <verse eid="COL 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="COL 2:12"/>
    You were buried with Him in baptism, through which you were also raised with Him through faith in the powerful working of God, who raised Him from death.
    <verse eid="COL 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="COL 2:13"/>
    When you were dead in your transgressions and in the uncircumcised state of your flesh, He made you alive together with Him, having forgiven us all our transgressions.
    <verse eid="COL 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="COL 2:14"/>
    He erased the written record of indebtedness that consisted of regulations that stood against us and were hostile to us, and He removed it completely by nailing it to the cross.
    <verse eid="COL 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="COL 2:15"/>
    After disarming the rulers and authorities, He displayed them publicly as conquered, having triumphed over them through Him.
    <verse eid="COL 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Holding Fast to Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="COL 2:16"/>
    Therefore, do not allow anyone to pass judgment on you regarding food or drink, or concerning a feast or new moon celebration or Sabbath observance.
    <verse eid="COL 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="COL 2:17"/>
    These are merely a shadow of what was coming, but the substance belongs to Christ.
    <verse eid="COL 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="COL 2:18"/>
    Let no one declare you disqualified by insisting on false humility and angel worship, dwelling on visions he claims to have seen, being groundlessly arrogant because of his unspiritual mindset,
    <verse eid="COL 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="COL 2:19"/>
    and failing to maintain connection with the Head, from whom the entire body, being supplied and held together through its joints and ligaments, experiences the growth that comes from God.
    <verse eid="COL 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="COL 2:20"/>
    If you died with Christ to the elementary principles of the world, why do you live as though you still belonged to the world by submitting to regulations:
    <verse eid="COL 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="COL 2:21"/>
    “Do not handle, do not taste, do not touch”
    <verse eid="COL 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="COL 2:22"/>
    (all these prohibitions refer to things destined to perish with use)—based on human commands and teachings?
    <verse eid="COL 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="COL 2:23"/>
    These regulations have an outward appearance of wisdom through self-directed religious practices and false humility and severe treatment of the body, but they possess no value in restraining indulgence of the flesh.
    <verse eid="COL 2:23"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="COL 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="COL 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Raised with Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="COL 3:1"/>
    Therefore, since you have been raised to new life with Christ, direct your pursuit towards the things above, where Christ is, seated at God’s right hand.
    <verse eid="COL 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="COL 3:2"/>
    Keep your minds focused on the things above, not on earthly matters.
    <verse eid="COL 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="COL 3:3"/>
    For you have died, and your life is now concealed with Christ in God.
    <verse eid="COL 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="COL 3:4"/>
    When Christ, who is your life, appears, then you also will appear with Him in glory.
    <verse eid="COL 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">New Life in Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="COL 3:5"/>
    Put to death, therefore, the earthly nature within you: sexual immorality, moral impurity, lustful passion, evil craving, and greed, which amounts to idolatry.
    <verse eid="COL 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="COL 3:6"/>
    Because of these practices, God’s wrath is coming upon those characterised by disobedience.
    <verse eid="COL 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="COL 3:7"/>
    You once conducted yourselves in these ways when you were living in that manner.
    <verse eid="COL 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="COL 3:8"/>
    But now you must also rid yourselves of all such things: anger, rage, malicious intent, slander, and obscene language from your mouth.
    <verse eid="COL 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="COL 3:9"/>
    Do not lie to one another, since you have stripped off the old self along with its practices,
    <verse eid="COL 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="COL 3:10"/>
    and have clothed yourselves with the new self that is being progressively renewed in knowledge according to the image of the One who created it.
    <verse eid="COL 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="COL 3:11"/>
    In this new reality there is no distinction between Greek and Jew, circumcised and uncircumcised, barbarian, Scythian, slave, or free person; rather, Christ is everything and is in everyone.
    <verse eid="COL 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="COL 3:12"/>
    Therefore, clothe yourselves as God's chosen ones, holy and dearly loved, with compassionate hearts, kindness, humility, gentleness, and patience,
    <verse eid="COL 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="COL 3:13"/>
    bearing with one another and extending forgiveness to each other. If anyone has a grievance against another, just as the Lord forgave you, you must do the same.
    <verse eid="COL 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="COL 3:14"/>
    And above all these qualities, clothe yourselves with love, which binds everything together in perfect harmony.
    <verse eid="COL 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="COL 3:15"/>
    Let the peace of Christ, to which you were indeed called as members of one body, govern your hearts; and cultivate gratitude.
    <verse eid="COL 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="COL 3:16"/>
    Let the word of Christ dwell among you abundantly, teaching and admonishing one another in all wisdom through psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs, singing to God with thankfulness in your hearts.
    <verse eid="COL 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="COL 3:17"/>
    And whatever you do, whether in word or action, do everything in the name of the Lord Jesus, expressing thanks to God the Father through Him.
    <verse eid="COL 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Christian Relationships</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="COL 3:18"/>
    Wives are to live in respectful submission to their husbands, as is appropriate for those who belong to the Lord.
    <verse eid="COL 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="COL 3:19"/>
    Husbands are to love their wives and avoid harshness or bitterness towards them.
    <verse eid="COL 3:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="COL 3:20"/>
    Children are to obey their parents in all things, since this delights the Lord.
    <verse eid="COL 3:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="COL 3:21"/>
    Fathers must not embitter their children, or they will become discouraged.
    <verse eid="COL 3:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="COL 3:22"/>
    Slaves, obey your earthly masters in all matters—not only when they are watching, as those who seek to please people, but with sincerity of heart, fearing the Lord.
    <verse eid="COL 3:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="COL 3:23"/>
    Whatever you do, work at it wholeheartedly, as serving the Lord rather than serving people,
    <verse eid="COL 3:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="COL 3:24"/>
    knowing that you will receive an inheritance as your reward from the Lord. Continue serving the Lord Christ.
    <verse eid="COL 3:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="COL 3:25"/>
    For the person who does wrong will be repaid for the wrong committed, and there is no partiality.
    <verse eid="COL 3:25"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="COL 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="COL 4"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="COL 4:1"/>
    Masters, provide what is fair and equitable to your slaves, recognising that you also have a Master in heaven.
    <verse eid="COL 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Further Injunctions</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="COL 4:2"/>
    Devote yourselves persistently to prayer, remaining alert in it with thanksgiving.
    <verse eid="COL 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="COL 4:3"/>
    Pray simultaneously for us as well, that God would open a door for us to proclaim the message, to speak the mystery of Christ, for which I have been imprisoned—
    <verse eid="COL 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="COL 4:4"/>
    so that I may declare it with clarity, as I am obligated to speak.
    <verse eid="COL 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="COL 4:5"/>
    Conduct yourselves with wisdom towards those outside the faith, making the most of every opportunity.
    <verse eid="COL 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="COL 4:6"/>
    Let your speech always be gracious, seasoned with salt, so you will know how to respond appropriately to each person.
    <verse eid="COL 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Fellow Workers in the Lord</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="COL 4:7"/>
    Tychicus, my dear brother and faithful servant and fellow worker in the Lord, will inform you about everything concerning my circumstances.
    <verse eid="COL 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="COL 4:8"/>
    I have sent him to you for this precise purpose: so that you may learn about our situation and so that he may encourage your hearts.
    <verse eid="COL 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="COL 4:9"/>
    He is coming with Onesimus, my faithful and dear brother, who is one of your own. They will tell you about everything happening here.
    <verse eid="COL 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="COL 4:10"/>
    Aristarchus, my fellow prisoner, sends you greetings, as does Mark, Barnabas’ cousin (you have received instructions about him; if he comes to you, welcome him),
    <verse eid="COL 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="COL 4:11"/>
    and Jesus who is called Justus. These are my only fellow workers for God’s kingdom who are from the circumcised community—they have been a source of comfort to me.
    <verse eid="COL 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="COL 4:12"/>
    Epaphras, who is one of your own, sends greetings. As a servant of Christ Jesus, he is always wrestling in prayer on your behalf, so that you may stand mature and completely assured in everything God wills.
    <verse eid="COL 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="COL 4:13"/>
    For I testify about him that he works hard for you and for those in Laodicea and Hierapolis.
    <verse eid="COL 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="COL 4:14"/>
    Luke, the beloved physician, sends greetings, as does Demas.
    <verse eid="COL 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="COL 4:15"/>
    Give my greetings to the brothers and sisters in Laodicea, and to Nympha and the church that meets in her house.
    <verse eid="COL 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="COL 4:16"/>
    After this letter has been read to your church, make sure it is also read in the church of the Laodiceans, and that you in turn read the letter from Laodicea.
    <verse eid="COL 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="COL 4:17"/>
    Tell Archippus: “Pay attention to the ministry you received in the Lord, so that you fulfil it completely.”
    <verse eid="COL 4:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Greeting and Benediction</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="COL 4:18"/>
    I, Paul, write this greeting with my own hand. Remember my imprisonment. Grace be with you.
    <verse eid="COL 4:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="COL 4"/>
</usx>
